# rocq-pi-leibniz: logical roots of the package.
# Content modules are carried verbatim from the submitted state
# (head 841855c); coq_makefile resolves the compile order.
#
# Two loadpath roots, order-sensitive (the later mapping wins for the
# directories it covers):
#   - "theories" is bound to "pi_leibniz" so the root re-export module is
#     reachable as pi_leibniz.PiLeibniz (the opam logpath);
#   - "theories/Reals/Cauchy" is then remapped to the empty root so every
#     content module keeps the bare logical name it was carried with
#     (the content files require each other by bare short name, e.g.
#     "Require Import PiKernelSlack.", and Rocq resolves Require by
#     exact logical name, not by suffix).

-Q theories pi_leibniz
-Q theories/Reals/Cauchy ""

# Engine file (abstract escape-window engine, reused unchanged)
theories/Reals/Cauchy/ConstructiveCauchyRealsSep.v

# Pi stack: five-file core plus nineteen-file supply layer
